WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.280
What if morality is just a fiction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:09.120
used by the herd of inferior human&nbsp;
beings to hold back the few superior men?

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.600
In this Sprouts special with&nbsp;
Stephen Hicks, we examine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.640
Nietzsche’s explanation for how ethics develop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:23.440
and the consequences for master types living in a&nbsp;
world that’s dominated by the morality of a slave.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.400
PART 3 “MASTER-SLAVE MORALITY and&nbsp;
the origin of the bad conscience

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.200
Nietzsche argued that there are two&nbsp;
explanations for how morality develops.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:47.360
Part of the story is bio-psychological —&nbsp;
in terms of what morality resonates with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:53.760
what psychological type of person one is. The&nbsp;
other part of the story is cultural, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:00.080
different moral codes develop under different&nbsp;
survival circumstances, and so Nietzsche searches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:06.000
history for the survival circumstances that&nbsp;
necessitated the development of slave morality

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.520
In the West, Nietzsche finds the slave&nbsp;
morality’s roots in the Judeo-Christian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:18.400
tradition–In a decisive set of events&nbsp;
that occurred early in Jewish history–the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.880
enslavement of the jews in Egypt. The&nbsp;
significant result of the Jews’ being enslaved&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.000
for a long time was the development&nbsp;
and internalization of a moral code&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.160
suitable for surviving slavery.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.200
Suppose that you are a slave: how do you&nbsp;
survive? And if you have children who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:46.480
born into slavery, what survival strategies will&nbsp;
you teach them? In order to survive, a slave must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:54.240
obey the master. This does not come naturally. So&nbsp;
the first lesson is: you must stifle your nature.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.360
Suppose the master strikes you — the desire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.360
for revenge comes naturally&nbsp;
— but you have to stifle it.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.200
Suppose the master tells you&nbsp;
to wait — being inactive does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.920
not come naturally — but you must&nbsp;
suppress your desire for activity.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.120
Suppose the master tells you&nbsp;
to do something you do not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:24.480
want to do — you must override your&nbsp;
desire to do what you want and obey.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:33.920
Generalizing, you must train yourself to restrain&nbsp;
your natural impulses and to internalize a humble,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.560
patient, obedient self. You know you must do&nbsp;
this because slaves who do not end up dead.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:50.160
Consequently, Nietzsche asserts, slave virtues&nbsp;
have survival value: obedience, humility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:56.480
forgiveness, and patience are good for slaves.&nbsp;
And those are the traits slaves will drill into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:03.840
Their children if they want them to survive. Over&nbsp;
time, the slave virtues become cultural values.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:12.560
In every generation many people are sheep-like&nbsp;
and do not especially mind being slaves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:17.840
But others resent it, and here the&nbsp;
story Nietzsche tells becomes darker.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.120
In order to survive they must direct&nbsp;
their natural strength and assertiveness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.480
against the expression of their&nbsp;
own strength and assertiveness.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:34.640
This naturally leads them to resent the&nbsp;
master strongly—but they also start to hate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.560
themselves for doing what the master says and&nbsp;
for their own role in suppressing themselves.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:49.840
Psychologically, hating oneself causes unbearable&nbsp;
pressure inside: because the outward discharge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:57.520
the instinct gets inhibited and turns backward&nbsp;
against man himself. Hostility, cruelty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.400
joy in destruction — all this turned&nbsp;
against the possessors of such instincts:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.760
that is the origin of the ‘bad conscience'

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:13.520
Hatred of the strong, self-hatred,&nbsp;
and revenge fantasies to ease the pain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:18.960
become the lived psychological reality&nbsp;
of such slaves. Make this psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:24.480
reality a matter of months and years, and&nbsp;
the results will be ugly and poisonous.

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.720
More provocatively, Nietzsche argues that such&nbsp;
slave individuals who feel the internal war most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:39.200
strongly become the social leaders of the slaves&nbsp;
— that is to say, they become their priests.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:45.280
“It is because of their impotence that in&nbsp;
them hatred grows to monstrous proportions.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:54.000
In their leadership role, it is the priests&nbsp;
who most strongly advocate meekness, humility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.520
and obedience —and who condemn the&nbsp;
aggressive strength and pride of the masters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.880
The priests are not in a position to&nbsp;
use physical power against the masters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:10.480
Instead the priests develop and use&nbsp;
morality as their weapon of confrontation.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:19.200
In the Judeo-Christian tradition, slave&nbsp;
morality becomes part of a revenge strategy. Its&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:23.440
point is to enable the weaker&nbsp;
to survive in a harsh world—but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:28.640
also to undermine the master type's&nbsp;
confidence in themselves and eventually&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.720
bring down the masters so as&nbsp;
to exact a spiritual revenge.

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:39.200
So: Strength, aggression, weakness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:44.560
resentment. Is morality really about&nbsp;
us getting along together in the world?&nbsp;

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:51.360
Or is it really a tool of power, a survival&nbsp;
strategy, and a way for the losers to strike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:57.520
back against the successful? Those are the&nbsp;
hard questions Nietzsche makes us live with.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:03.040
THE END

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.720
What are your thoughts on morality?&nbsp;
Do you agree with Nietzsche?&nbsp;

